// - Rust's `(0..5).collect::<Vec<_>>()` works directly: `0..5` is a
//   range expression that evaluates to `RangeI32` in Logos, and
//   `.collect::<Vec<i32>>()` flows through CP-cm-14 / FromIterator.
// - Vec equality replaced with per-index assertion (no Vec PartialEq).
